# Fine Hub — Tailwind CSS

Tailwind v4 is enabled via `app/globals.css` (`@import 'tailwindcss'`).

## Rules

1. **No raw default link UI** — never ship bare `<Link>text</Link>` without styling. Use `HubBackLink` or Tailwind link/button classes.
2. **New UI and refactors** — use Tailwind utility classes. Map colors to CSS tokens: `bg-[var(--surface)]`, `text-[var(--muted)]`, `border-[var(--line)]`.
3. **Legacy CSS** — existing `app/styles/*.css` remains for internal board, panels, modals. Settings/admin pages use `personal-hub-*` + `hub-page` patterns first.
4. **Buttons** — reuse `.appdev-btn-primary`, `.appdev-btn-ghost`, `.appdev-btn-danger` until migrated.
5. **Dark theme** — always use `var(--*)` tokens, not hardcoded hex, so `[data-theme="dark"]` keeps working.
6. **Shared primitives** — put reusable Tailwind components in `components/ui/` (e.g. `HubBackLink`).

## Examples

```jsx
// Back nav
<HubBackLink href="/me" label="Personal hub" />

// Card
<div className="rounded-[var(--radius-lg)] border border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--surface)] p-5" />
```
